BT
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 312 Tm
(4. What is Redpanda?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 293 Tm
(Redpanda is a streaming platform that speaks the Kafka protocol. Producers and consumers) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 280 Tm
(use the same Kafka client libraries, but Redpanda is a single binary \(no ZooKeeper/KRaft) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 267 Tm
(ops overhead\), which makes local Kubernetes setup much simpler than Apache Kafka.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 254 Tm
(- Redpanda = the message bus / buffer between the simulator and the database.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 241 Tm
(- It holds recent KPI events in topics until ingest workers catch up.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 228 Tm
(- It is NOT the long-term analytics store.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 215 Tm
(- Later you can swap Redpanda for Amazon MSK / Confluent Cloud without rewriting) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 202 Tm
(   producers/consumers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 185 Tm
(5. How Data Injection \(Simulation\) Works) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 166 Tm
(We do not pull from real routers in v1. A Python service kpi-simulator generates fake) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 153 Tm
(but realistic network telemetry and publishes it to Kafka/Redpanda.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 140 Tm
(- Config: number of devices, metrics per device, target messages/sec, fault injection) Tj
ET
endstream
